WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.143
The future rarely unfolds exactly as expected.

2
00:00:03.143 --> 00:00:10.996
Structured techniques encourage analysts to explore alternative futures and identify factors that could lead to different outcomes.

3
00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:13.450
This work often begins with key assumptions.

4
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.581
If a major assumption changes, what paths become more likely?

5
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:22.012
What early indicators would suggest movement toward one path instead of another?

6
00:00:22.012 --> 00:00:27.041
Considering multiple possibilities improves preparedness and reduces overconfidence.

7
00:00:27.041 --> 00:00:32.868
It helps teams plan for uncertainty instead of treating one forecast as the only plausible outcome.

8
00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.302
The objective is not precise prediction.

9
00:00:35.302 --> 00:00:41.299
The objective is understanding what could happen, why it could happen, and how organizations might respond.
